======================================================================================================================
G2 -- is f_DM prior-driven?  (RC41 overlap, actual SED + gas)
======================================================================================================================
  Delta_prior = log M_bar,fit - log(M* + M_gas): median -0.100 dex (n = 38); Spearman rho(delta_flat, Delta_prior) = +0.28 (p = 0.093)
  Theil-Sen slope of delta_flat on Delta_prior +0.128; z-slope of delta_flat after removing it: +0.009 [-0.044, +0.075] (n = 38)
  -> prior-driven (|rho| >= 0.3 and p < 0.05): no

======================================================================================================================
G3 -- the pressure term (V_c'^2 = V_c^2 - (3.36 - alpha) sigma0^2; g_bar fixed)
======================================================================================================================
  alpha = 3.36 (n = 100)             flat: slope -0.029 [-0.071, +0.002] (z: flat-true -1.6, rival-true -5.5); rival: slope -0.092 [-0.128, -0.055] (z: flat-true -1.7, rival-true -4.9)
  alpha = 1.68 (n = 100)             flat: slope -0.067 [-0.112, -0.028] (z: flat-true -3.2, rival-true -7.0); rival: slope -0.124 [-0.163, -0.083] (z: flat-true -2.9, rival-true -6.1)
  alpha = 0.0: 2 galaxies have V_c'^2 <= 0 (the fit's pressure term exceeds V_c^2) and are excluded from this variant
  alpha = 0.0 (n = 98)               flat: slope -0.098 [-0.140, -0.053] (z: flat-true -4.4, rival-true -8.0); rival: slope -0.149 [-0.194, -0.106] (z: flat-true -3.5, rival-true -6.4)
  the rival's deficit survives: alpha 3.36: YES; alpha 1.68: YES; alpha 0.0: YES

