======================================================================================================================
G5 -- can a z-dependent gas mis-scaling ALONE produce the pattern?  g_bar,analysis = g_bar,true x 10^(beta log10((1 + z)/2.5))
======================================================================================================================
  [PASS] C4 machinery: the flat-truth mock at beta = 0 gives slopes (0, expected) equal to the baseline expectations to 1e-9
         +0.00e+00, -0.059574 vs -0.059574
  M1 (flat truth): the mis-scaling that reproduces the observed delta_flat slope -0.029: beta = +0.216 -> differential dlog M_bar (z 0.6 -> 2.5) = +0.074 dex; the rival's slope there -0.086 (observed -0.092)
  M2 (rival truth): best beta = +0.762 (dlog M_bar = +0.259 dex) with chi2 = 0.02 (slopes -0.031, -0.090 vs observed -0.029, -0.092); within the plausible range |dlog M_bar| <= 0.2 dex (|beta| <= 0.59): best chi2 = 3.14 at beta = +0.58; at beta = 0: chi2 = 54.9
  -> M2 produces the pattern at a plausible mis-scaling (chi2 < 2 with |dlog M_bar| <= 0.2 dex): no; the stress variant V1 (gas fraction fixed with z) corresponds to about -0.18 dex of differential M_bar

======================================================================================================================
G7 -- regress delta on log g_bar first (Theil-Sen), then the z-slope of the residuals
======================================================================================================================
  flat : slope on log g_bar -0.053 [-0.115, +0.013]; residual z-slope -0.027 [-0.060, +0.007] (expected if flat true +0.000, if rival true +0.072; z: -1.6 / -5.8)
  rival: slope on log g_bar +0.000 [-0.073, +0.080]; residual z-slope -0.092 [-0.125, -0.055] (expected if flat true -0.067, if rival true +0.000; z: -1.4 / -5.2)
  -> the rival's residual z-slope stays negative (CI upper < 0): YES

======================================================================================================================
DECISION ROWS (frozen, with addendum 1)
======================================================================================================================
  D2 gas prior: survives V2-V5 (the plausible variants): False; survives V1 (the stress variant): False
  D2 pressure: survives alpha = 1.68 and 0: True
  G4: gas-scaling-sensitive negative flat slope: None
  D3 (headline): CFG216's outcome is ATTACK-BROKEN

  NOTE (written after the numbers above were seen): the literal D3 is driven by G1 on the 38-galaxy RC41 overlap, where even V0 (the baseline)
  fails the survival rule (the deficit is not significant in that subsample: CFG216's own sensitivity (a) has the same weakness). So G1's frozen version
  cannot discriminate, and the literal ATTACK-BROKEN is a power artefact, not evidence against the deficit. The informative rows are G3, G5 and G7 and the post hoc block below.

